provider: ollama-cloud (glm-5.3)
request: Add a clear command that removes todos whose completed field is true.

single call 1: edit -> src/types.ts, src/commands.ts, src/commands.test.ts  (Added a `clear` command that removes todos whose completed status is true. The request's "completed field" maps to this codebase's `Todo.done` field (there is no `completed` field anywhere in the repo), so `clear(todos)` filters out entries with `done === true`. Wiring: new `{ kind: "clear" }` variant in the `Command` union, `parseArgs(["clear"])` returns it, and `run` persists the filtered list and reports how many were removed (`Cleared N todo(s)`). Added new unit tests for clear(), parseArgs, and run-against-file behaviour; no existing tests were changed or removed.)
round 1: oracle GREEN
single call 2: accept  (The clear command is implemented and the oracle is green (tsc --noEmit exit 0; vitest 12/12 passed). `clear` filters out todos with done === true (the codebase's completion field; the request's "completed field" has no literal counterpart in the repo), it is wired into the Command union, parseArgs, and run (which persists the pruned list and reports "Cleared N todo(s)"), and it is covered by new tests without touching any existing ones.)

